%N A400763 Numbers k such that the k-th composition in standard order is a palindrome. Positions of palindromes in A066099.
%C A400763 First differs from A329395 in lacking 166.
%C A400763 Palindromes or symmetric compositions are counted by A016116.
%C A400763 The k-th composition in standard order (graded reverse-lexicographic, A066099) is obtained by taking the set of positions of 1's in the reversed binary expansion of k, prepending 0, taking first differences, and reversing again. This gives a bijective correspondence between nonnegative integers and integer compositions.
%H A400763 Gus Wiseman, <a href="https://docs.google.com/document/d/e/2PACX-1vTCPiJVFUXN8IqfLlCXkgP15yrGWeRhFS4ozST5oA4Bl2PYS-XTA3sGsAEXvwW-B0ealpD8qnoxFqN3/pub">Statistics, classes, and transformations of standard compositions</a>
%F A400763 a(n) = A044051(n) - 1.
%e A400763 The 148-th composition is (3,2,3), which is a palindrome, so 148 is in the sequence.
%e A400763 The 166-th composition is (2,3,1,2), which is not a palindrome, so 166 is not in the sequence.
%e A400763 The terms together with corresponding palindromes begin:
%e A400763     0: ()
%e A400763     1: (1)
%e A400763     2: (2)
%e A400763     3: (1,1)
%e A400763     4: (3)
%e A400763     7: (1,1,1)
%e A400763     8: (4)
%e A400763    10: (2,2)
%e A400763    13: (1,2,1)
%e A400763    15: (1,1,1,1)
%e A400763    16: (5)
%e A400763    22: (2,1,2)
%e A400763    25: (1,3,1)
%e A400763    31: (1,1,1,1,1)
%e A400763    32: (6)
%e A400763    36: (3,3)
%e A400763    42: (2,2,2)
%e A400763    46: (2,1,1,2)
%e A400763    49: (1,4,1)
%e A400763    53: (1,2,2,1)
%e A400763    59: (1,1,2,1,1)
%e A400763    63: (1,1,1,1,1,1)
%t A400763 stc[n_]:= Differences[Prepend[Join @@ Position[Reverse[IntegerDigits[n,2]],1],0]]//Reverse;
%t A400763 Select[Range[0,100], stc[#]==Reverse[stc[#]]&]
%Y A400763 For binary expansion we have A006995 (see also A044051), complement A154809.
%Y A400763 These compositions are counted by A016116.
%Y A400763 For conjugate partitions we have A088902, counted by A000700.
%Y A400763 For just first = last we have A400764, counted by A128209.
%Y A400763 The case of even length is A400765, counted by A077957.
%Y A400763 The case of odd length is A400766, counted by A016116.
%Y A400763 A000740 counts aperiodic compositions, ranks A328594.
%Y A400763 A003242 counts anti-run compositions, ranks A333489.
%Y A400763 A005811 counts runs in binary expansion.
%Y A400763 A011782 counts compositions.
%Y A400763 A032020 counts strict compositions, ranks A233564.
%Y A400763 A059893 reverses standard composition.
%Y A400763 A066099 lists compositions in standard order.
%Y A400763 A098124 counts compositions with max part = length, ranks A389532.
%Y A400763 A000005 counts constant compositions, ranks A272919.
%Y A400763 A353860 counts collapsible compositions, ranks A354908.
%Y A400763 Cf. A001045, A029837, A044813, A059966, A091065, A098504, A124767, A238130, A329395, A389530, A390675.
